# Memory layer 3 of https://cho.sh/ko/1983DC, set on the owner's ask of 2026-10-19. Installed as /etc/default/earlyoom.
# SIGTERM the process with the highest oom_score when both available RAM and free swap fall under 5%, SIGKILL under 2%.
# The regexes match /proc/<pid>/comm. Node processes all read node-MainThread, so the chat service and pi-pool (python3)
# are kept by oom-protect.py's -900 score instead, and heavy-wrapped test runners are picked first by their score of 500.
# The CI guests (qemu:ci-*) are avoided, which subtracts 300: on 10-26 from 02:22 to 02:27Z a fork run of agent commands
# filled RAM and swap, and with the guests preferred (+300, about 990 against 800 for an adj-200 agent command) earlyoom
# SIGTERMed 6 running guests, about 51 GB, and the shortage went on. Avoided, a guest reads about 390, under every
# adj-200 process and still over the Prime workers (-500, about 334) and the harness core (-900, about 68).
# -N runs oom-kill-session.py after each kill, which kills the rest of the agent command session oom-protect.py marked
# at 1000 (about 1333, over every other score), because earlyoom picks one process at a time.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 5,2 -s 5,2 -r 3600 -N /usr/local/lib/oom-protect/oom-kill-session.py --avoid '^(systemd|systemd-.+|init|sshd|sshd-session|tailscaled|dockerd|containerd|containerd-shim.*|earlyoom|prime-agent|pi-pool|qemu:ci-.+)$' --prefer '^(qemu-system-.+|vitest.*|jest.*|pytest|svelte-check|tsc|cc1plus|ld)$'"
